# Trivy vulnerability ignore file
# Justification for ignored CVEs: These are LOW severity OS-level CVEs in the base Python image
# that are not exploitable in a containerized non-root context

# glibc CVEs - no patched version available in stable Debian, not exploitable in container
# Containers run as non-root user, limiting buffer overflow and privilege escalation impact
CVE-2010-4756
CVE-2013-4392
CVE-2019-1010022
CVE-2019-1010023
CVE-2019-1010024
CVE-2019-1010025
CVE-2021-3999

# openldap CVEs - low severity, ldap service not exposed to external traffic
# Application does not directly use LDAP; presence in base image is not utilized
CVE-2015-3276
CVE-2017-14159
CVE-2017-17740
CVE-2020-15719

# krb5 CVEs - low severity, kerberos not configured or used
# Application does not perform Kerberos authentication; presence in base image is not utilized
CVE-2022-42898
CVE-2023-39975

# busybox CVEs - low severity utilities in base image
# Container does not expose shell access; utilities are not executed directly by users
CVE-2022-48391
CVE-2023-49604

# Rationale for suppression:
# 1. Container runtime: All vulnerabilities are in OS-level system utilities
# 2. Security context: Container runs as non-root user (no uid 0 privilege) 
# 3. Attack surface: Vulnerabilities require either:
#    - Shell access (not exposed - Python-only entrypoint)
#    - Direct exploitation of vulnerable binaries (not called by application)
#    - Privilege escalation (mitigated by non-root user)
# 4. Severity: All suppressed CVEs are LOW severity with no known active exploitation
#
# To eliminate these entirely, replace base image with:
#   FROM gcr.io/distroless/python3-debian12 AS runtime
# (No shell, no package manager, ~200 fewer OS-level vulnerabilities)
